        <p>Most of my work falls into three buckets: <strong>WordPress builds</strong> for orgs that need them done right, <strong>Salesforce integrations</strong> that actually sync, and <strong>custom tools</strong> when the off-the-shelf thing doesn't fit.</p>
        <p>I work directly. No account managers, no project managers, no handoffs. You talk to the person building the thing — which means decisions get made faster, scope stays honest, and the work shows up the way it was supposed to.</p>
        <p>Some of that direct work is with clients. Some of it is embedded with web and marketing agencies as senior dev capacity — white-label or co-branded, project-based or ongoing. Either way, the engagement is designed around the work, not the org chart.</p>
        <p>Two decades in. One hundred-plus custom sites and tools launched. Seven of those years at the National Organization for Rare Disorders, building RareDiseases.org and twenty patient registry microsites. The rest spent building for everyone from craft breweries to state governments to international institutions.</p>
